     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;color:black;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Raja undulata is an\r\nimportant fishery resource in Portuguese waters. Currently data required for\r\nestimating abundance of the species is derived from a self-sampling program\r\nconducted by fishermen. </span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;color:black;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">The information collected\r\nnumber of specimens caught by fishing haul and geographic coordinates of the\r\nfishing haul. Previously fishermen also provided data of hauls for which no\r\nspecimens of </span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;color:black;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Raja undulata was\r\ncollected. Using former data N-mixture models were applied to get abundance\r\nestimates as well as estimates of detection probability (</span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/316679852_Estimating_animal_abundance_with_N-mixture_models_using_the_R-INLA_package_for_R\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/316679852_Estimating_animal_abundance_with_N-mixture_models_using_the_R-INLA_package_for_R&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792441552887000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Bh-MA-ownNusWaede8VaT\">https://www.researchgate.net/publication/316679852_Estimating_animal_abundance_with_N-mixture_models_using_the_R-INLA_package_for_R</a></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;color:black;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">). </span><span style=\"color:#212121\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica,sans-serif;color:black;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Regarding more recent\r\ndata for which only  positive fishing haul ae available, i.e., fishing\r\nhauls where the species was caught, we would like to know if there are\r\nmethodological procedures in line with this change. </span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:13.3333px\">Waiting to hear from you Thanks</span></font></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#1f497d\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#212121\"><u></u><u></u></span></p></div>"
